  "title": "Si-o-se-pol (Allahverdi Khan Bridge)",
  "summary": "Si-o-se-pol, the Bridge of 33 Arches, also called the Allahverdi Khan Bridge, is a double-deck brick-and-stone arch bridge over the Zayandeh River in Isfahan. Built between 1599 and 1602 on the order of Shah Abbas I, with Allahverdi Khan overseeing the work, it is Isfahan's longest bridge and has long served as a public gathering place.",
